@@ -0,0 +1,57 @@
+# Logging and ops alerts
+
+Observability has three lanes. Pick the lane by *why* the event matters, not by its severity.
+
+| Lane | Destination | Retention | Use it for | Entry point |
+| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |
+| **Archive** | `storage/logs/laravel.log` (daily rotation) | `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` (default 14) | Routine application logs, debug to error, troubleshooting | `Log::debug/info/warning/error(...)` (default `stack`) |
+| **Audit** | `storage/logs/audit.log` (daily rotation) | `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` (default 90), min level `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` (default `info`) | Durable "who changed what / who tried what" trail | `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` |
+| **Alert** | Discord incoming webhook | Discord's history | Human-pageable ops incidents | `App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send(...)` |
+
+## Decision guide (developers and agents)
+
+1. **Did a person or system change business state or security-relevant access?**
+   Membership role changes, subscription status transitions, login lockouts, plan limit changes.
+   → **Audit**: `Log::channel('audit')->info('Subscription status changed', [...])`.
+2. **Does someone need to be woken up now?**
+   A job that exhausted its retries, a payment-gateway webhook failing, a plan limit blocking an entity.
+   → **Alert**: call `DiscordOpsAlert::send()` explicitly from the code that detected the incident.
+3. **Anything else** (routine events, handled errors, debugging context).
+   → **Archive**: the default `Log::` facade.
+
+Rules that follow from the lanes:
+
+- **Discord is not a log channel.** There is no `discord` Monolog channel and none should be added. Never send to Discord through `Log::`.
+- An alert is not a record. If an incident should be kept, also write it to the archive (or audit) lane.
+- Audit entries are written at `info` or above. Keep debug detail out of the audit file.
+- Never log or alert secrets or personal data. `DiscordOpsAlert` redacts keys such as `password`, `token`, `secret`, `authorization`, `api_key` and `webhook`, and any string containing `Bearer <credential>`. Treat that as a safety net, not permission to pass secrets.
+- Logs do not leave the server. Shipping them to an external service is out of scope.
+
+## Archive and audit channels
+
+Both are `daily` channels, so each writes a dated file, for example `audit-2026-10-29.log`, and deletes files older than its retention.
+
+The default `stack` channel is `LOG_STACK` (default `daily`), which writes to the archive lane. The audit lane is **not** part of the stack; it only receives writes made to it explicitly.
+
+## Discord ops alerts
+
+`App\Ops\DiscordOpsAlert::send(string $title, string $message, array $context = [])`:
+
+- **No-op** when `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` is empty or unset: no HTTP request is made. Local and test environments leave it empty.
+- Sends `POST` with a JSON body `{"content": "<text>"}` to the configured URL, with a 5-second timeout.
+- Text is the title, the message, then one `key=value` line per context entry (nested arrays are rendered as JSON). It is cut to **1800 characters**, under Discord's 2000-character limit.
+- **Soft-fail**: it never throws. A non-2xx answer or a transport error is written to the archive lane as an `error` entry, `Discord ops alert failed`, with the status code or exception class. The webhook URL is never logged, because it embeds the token.
+- Not yet wired into jobs, webhooks or exception handlers. Those call sites are added per incident type.
+
+## Configuration
+
+| Env key | Default | Purpose |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `LOG_STACK` | `daily` | Channels behind the default `stack` |
+| `LOG_LEVEL` | `debug` | Level for the archive (`daily`) channel |
+| `LOG_DAILY_DAYS` | `14` | Archive retention in days |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_LEVEL` | `info` | Minimum level written to the audit file |
+| `LOG_AUDIT_DAYS` | `90` | Audit retention in days |
+| `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL` | empty | Discord incoming webhook. Empty disables alerts |
+
+`phpunit.xml` pins `LOG_STACK=daily` and an empty `DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL`, so the test suite does not depend on a local `.env` and never posts to Discord.
